# Target C — audited §151 outer-walk surplus from the harmonic diameter moment

**Date:** 2026-09-12  
**Lifecycle:** audited-working proof-only route module; theorem-state authority unchanged.  
**LEVEL I STATUS:** **STILL OPEN. C-II REMAINS OPEN.**

This module extracts the one live general consequence from the older gap-moment branch that is not already contained in normalized §§140 and 148–150. The historical scalar endpoint `h/D=1.721247...` is already excluded by normalized §146, so the associated endpoint-only two-edge-tooth density theorem is not retained as an active research section.

Let

\[
U_D:=u_B
\]

be the Type-II extra outer-walk surplus, so after the centralized loaded-contact localization

\[
b=q+m+u_B,
\]

where `b` is the occurrence-counted outer contact-walk length and `m` is the number of nonunit loaded force-hull sides. Let

\[
S_D:=\sum_r d_r
\]

be the total harmonic-cell diameter moment, and put

\[
c_*:={\pi\over4}(2-\sqrt3).
\]

Then every sufficiently large Type-II survivor satisfies

\[
\boxed{
U_D
\ge
\pi D-{5\over2}(h-s_Z)
+{1\over2}S_D
+{c_*\over2}D
-o(D).
}
\tag{151.1}
\]

Equivalently, for any subsequence on which

\[
S_D\ge(S-o(1))D,
\]

\[
\boxed{
{u_B\over D}
\ge
\pi-{5\over2}{h-s_Z\over D}
+{1\over2}(S+c_*)-o(1).
}
\tag{151.2}
\]

This is a genuine all-regime Type-II tradeoff. It does **not** assume saturation of the weaker historical `h/D=1.721247...` endpoint.

---

## 151.1 Proof

Type-II near-disk convergence gives

\[
\operatorname{per}(F)=\pi D+o(D).
\tag{151.3}
\]

The occurrence-counted outer contact walk dominates the force-hull perimeter, so

\[
b\ge\operatorname{per}(F).
\]

Using `b=q+m+u_B`,

\[
\boxed{
u_B\ge\pi D-q-m-o(D).}
\tag{151.4}
\]

Normalized §148 gives the audited weighted component/payment inequality

\[
3q-2m-5k
\ge
S_D+c_*D-o(D),
\qquad k=d_H+s_Z.
\tag{151.5}
\]

Solve (151.5) for `m`:

\[
m
\le
{3q-5k-S_D-c_*D\over2}+o(D).
\tag{151.6}
\]

Insert (151.6) into (151.4):

\[
\begin{aligned}
u_B
&\ge
\pi D-q
-{3q-5k-S_D-c_*D\over2}
-o(D)\\
&=
\pi D-{5\over2}(q-k)
+{1\over2}S_D
+{c_*\over2}D
-o(D).
\end{aligned}
\]

Since

\[
q-k=(h+d_H)-(d_H+s_Z)=h-s_Z,
\]

this is exactly (151.1).

No sign reversal occurs: the upper bound for `m` is substituted into the negative term `-m` in (151.4), producing a lower bound for `u_B`.

---

## 151.2 Endpoint/common-cap specialization

On the repaired §140 Section-118 endpoint/common-cap branch,

\[
S_D\ge(S_*-o(1))D,
\qquad
S_*=2.798596312209462\ldots .
\]

Therefore

\[
{u_B\over D}
\ge
\pi-{5\over2}{h-s_Z\over D}
+{1\over2}(S_*+c_*)-o(1).
\tag{151.7}
\]

This specialization is valid only in that endpoint/common-cap branch. The general theorem (151.1) uses the actual diameter moment `S_D` and has no Section-118 endpoint hypothesis.

The older draft substituted the scalar lower edge

\[
h/D=1.721247148\ldots,
\qquad s_Z=o(D),
\]

and obtained `u_B/D>=0.342996...`. That endpoint is no longer live because normalized §146 proves the stronger general Type-II floor

\[
\liminf h/D\ge1.8195135379794445\ldots .
\]

Accordingly the historical endpoint-only tooth-density theorem built on `h/D->1.721247...` is mathematically consistent but vacuous in the current audited stack and is not assigned a new section number.

---

## 151.3 Scope

- All source points are retained; no contact-isolated coordinate is inserted into the core affine-kernel theorem.
- Occurrence multiplicity is retained in `b` and `u_B`.
- The result uses only Type-II perimeter convergence and the already audited §148 weighted payment.
- A positive lower bound on `u_B/D` requires a sufficiently strong lower bound on `S_D/D` together with an upper/endpoint control on `(h-s_Z)/D`; (151.1) itself is only a tradeoff.
- No claim is made that linear outer-walk surplus alone closes C-II.

**Disposition:** audited-working proof-only theorem. C-II and Level I remain open.
